DS mode: boot DSi-enhanced carts through the DS path

On DS hardware a DSi-enhanced cart (header unitcode bit 1) still runs
in DS mode. melonDS set the DSi cart-ID bit unconditionally and, with
DirectBoot, took the DSi boot path (NWRAM/MBK setup from the DSi header
region), which stalls without DSi BIOS/NAND: uniform white screens.
Gate both decisions on the console type so DS mode matches real DS
hardware. Fixes Pokemon White 2 (and other DSi-enhanced carts) hanging
on a white screen in game nds.

--- a/src/DSi.cpp
+++ b/src/DSi.cpp
@@ -296,8 +296,9 @@
 {
     bool dsmode = false;
 
-    // TODO: add controls for forcing DS or DSi mode?
-    if (!(NDSCart::Header.UnitCode & 0x02))
+    // DSi-enhanced carts run in DS mode on DS hardware: boot them
+    // through the DS path, not the DSi one (which needs DSi BIOS/NAND).
+    if (!(NDSCart::Header.UnitCode & 0x02) || NDS::ConsoleType == 0)
         dsmode = true;
 
     // TODO: RAM size!!
--- a/src/NDSCart.cpp
+++ b/src/NDSCart.cpp
@@ -1549,7 +1549,8 @@
                    (u32)Header.GameCode[0];
 
     u8 unitcode = Header.UnitCode;
-    CartIsDSi = (unitcode & 0x02) != 0;
+    // In DS mode the cart answers like a plain DS cart (no DSi ID bit).
+    CartIsDSi = (unitcode & 0x02) != 0 && Config::ConsoleType != 0;
 
     ROMListEntry romparams;
     if (!ReadROMParams(gamecode, &romparams))
